1
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:19,520
♪ I notice every glance ♪

2
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,520
♪ The way you look at me ♪

3
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:29,160
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

4
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:32,800
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,000
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

6
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:40,160
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

7
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:43,480
♪ But the closer we get ♪

8
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:47,440
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

9
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:52,240
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

10
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,360
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

11
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:57,800
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

12
00:00:58,360 --> 00:00:59,800
Mr. Sam has caused trouble again.

13
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,080
Again?

14
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,680
Find a new nurse as soon as possible.

15
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,520
I've been playing nice for so long.

16
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,800
But in the end,

17
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:09,160
you just can't afford it.

18
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,920
I'd like to turn down this job.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,520
You have to pay a penalty
of five times your salary.

20
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,960
I'll work the full 120 days.

21
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,080
Prepare to fall apart,

22
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,440
Uttawadee.

23
00:01:37,479 --> 00:01:38,800
I'll leave it to you, Cream.

24
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,360
Uh…

25
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,520
Are you okay, Oh?

26
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:01,480
Hello, Dr. Smith.

27
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,480
Are you going upstairs to check on Madam?

28
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,160
No.

29
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,400
I'm just bringing Oh here today.

30
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:10,039
Cream,

31
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,360
this is Oh.

32
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,720
She's a registered nurse

33
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,800
from the neurology department,

34
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,079
specializing in caring for patients

35
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,640
with Alzheimer's and paralysis.

36
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:21,920
Hello, Ms. Oh.

37
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,200
Hello.

38
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:26,280
You can head back now, Doctor.

39
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,840
I'll go over the job details with Ms. Oh.

40
00:02:33,079 --> 00:02:35,200
You were supposed to start tomorrow, right?

41
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,280
Or can you start this evening?

42
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,480
Yes, that's fine.

43
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,560
Mrs. Pinthong usually wakes up around 7 a.m.

44
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:54,040
The housekeepers prepare breakfast at 7:30.

45
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,160
After Madam has breakfast
and takes her medication,

46
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,200
you'll usually take her out to the garden
for some fresh air

47
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,760
for about half an hour to an hour.

48
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,280
After that, she likes being read to.

49
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,160
Is there anything else she likes

50
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,000
besides being read to?

51
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,680
Listening to music.

52
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,160
She likes having someone play music for her.

53
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,680
As for the other members of the household,

54
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,280
there's Ms. Nueng, Ms. Song's older sister.

55
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:21,800
She's very kind,

56
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,520
so if anything is bothering you,
you can talk to her.

57
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,560
But only if she's in the mood.

58
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,560
Then there's Mr. Sam, the youngest brother.

59
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,800
Avoid him if you can.

60
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,680
I've heard about him from Smith.

61
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,960
You've already met Ms. Song.

62
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,560
She's the middle child.

63
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,360
She's gone back to work already.

64
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,400
She's very busy,

65
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,160
so she doesn't come home often.

66
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,760
And Mr. Methanee…

67
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,280
has passed away.

68
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,240
This way, please.

69
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:18,440
Thank you.

70
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,680
This is Madam's room.

71
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:31,040
Wok.

72
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,800
Pork.

73
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:35,200
Vegetables. Delicious dipping sauce.

74
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,040
She's watching TV.

75
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,480
Do you have any questions, Ms. Oh?

76
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:49,960
No.

77
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,040
Then let's get your bags

78
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,400
and take you to your room.

79
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,280
This way, please.

80
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,520
This is your room.

81
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,840
If you need anything, just let me know.

82
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,840
Okay.

83
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,520
Right, I almost forgot something.

84
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,320
Yes?

85
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:18,080
Please wear your regular clothes
while you're working here.

86
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:20,600
We don't want Madam
to feel like she's a patient.

87
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:24,680
And the nurse I saw earlier?

88
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:27,120
She's a part-time nurse.

89
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,240
I see.

90
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,960
Ms. Cream,

91
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,960
you don't have to be so formal with me.

92
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,520
Just call me Oh.

93
00:05:35,159 --> 00:05:36,080
Sure.

94
00:05:36,159 --> 00:05:39,480
Then just call me Cream.
We're probably around the same age anyway.

95
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:41,000
Okay.

96
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,080
I'll get back to work now.

97
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,680
Thank you.

98
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,960
OH

99
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,880
Hey, Oh! How's it going?

100
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,120
Is your employer treating you okay?

101
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,960
Well… sort of.

102
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:09,600
Ong,

103
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:12,680
they want me to dress casually here. No uniform.

104
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,560
Send me the address.

105
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,240
I'll ship some clothes over.

106
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,640
They'll look stunning on you!

107
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,080
Thank you, Miss Seller.

108
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:23,280
So, how's Mom?

109
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,560
Her condition is stable.

110
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:28,040
I'm keeping a close eye on her,

111
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,560
so don't worry.

112
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:30,960
Okay.

113
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,000
Mm-hmm.

114
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,960
Good.

115
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:33,960
Bye-bye.

116
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,240
A printer?

117
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,560
That's right.

118
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,160
Could you help me?

119
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,080
Oh, sure.

120
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,000
Send me the file, and I'll take care of it.

121
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,920
Is it a document?

122
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,320
It's a set of photos.

123
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,400
Uh…

124
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,920
These are photos of the family members.

125
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,640
What are you going to use them for?

126
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,440
It's one of the brain-training activities.

127
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,440
I see.

128
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,040
What do you think you're doing?

129
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,320
Ms. Kasira?

130
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,320
First night here,

131
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,360
and you're already trying to hurt the homeowner?

132
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,440
I thought you were a thief!

133
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:46,400
My house has tight security.

134
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,240
A thief wouldn't get in so easily.

135
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,240
How was I supposed to know?

136
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:53,080
Besides, I didn't expect you to come home.

137
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,640
Why? Can't I come back to my own house?

138
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,880
I thought you usually stay somewhere else.

139
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,160
That's my business.

140
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,880
Whether I come back or not

141
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,960
has nothing to do with you.

142
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,040
Or…

143
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,240
are you offering me a special service?

144
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,040
If you want a designer bag,

145
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:28,040
I can get you one.

146
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:32,080
Thank you,

147
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:33,880
but you can keep it.

148
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,880
I'm here as a nurse

149
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,920
to take care of your mother.

150
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,360
Did you really think I'd trust you
to take care of my mother?

151
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,840
If you don't trust me,

152
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,400
why are you keeping me here?

153
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,880
Don't put it that way.

154
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:53,560
Someone like you isn't worth keeping around.

155
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,600
I just need someone to care for my mother.

156
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,440
Then you can rest assured.

157
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,720
For the next 120 days,

158
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:09,280
your mother will be well cared for.

159
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,640
Make sure you live up to that.

160
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,520
Don't just say things to fool people.

161
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:22,800
I won't let even the slightest mistake slide.

162
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,120
Good morning, ma'am.

163
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,160
Who are you?

164
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,320
It's me, Cream.

165
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:12,920
No, please don't!

166
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,120
It's me, Cream.

167
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,160
Porn's daughter, remember?

168
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,040
Porn's daughter?

169
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,120
Yes.

170
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,080
No,

171
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,680
you don't look like her.

172
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:26,240
I do look like her.

173
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,360
I've just grown up and gotten prettier.

174
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:33,160
Okay, how about this?

175
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,080
You'll definitely remember this!

176
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,640
♪ The chicken is being grilled!

177
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:39,880
♪ The chicken is being grilled! ♪

178
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,440
♪ It'll be skewered, yeah! ♪

179
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,800
♪ It'll be skewered, yeah! ♪

180
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:44,160
♪ On the left bottom! ♪

181
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,400
♪ On the right bottom! ♪

182
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:48,080
♪ So hot, so hot, so hot! ♪

183
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,320
It really is you, Cream.

184
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,600
I'm glad you're here.

185
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,400
Help me sit up.

186
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:58,600
Of course.

187
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,480
Ma'am,

188
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:02,920
this is Ms. Oh.

189
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,800
She'll be helping to take care of you.

190
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,680
I'll take it from here.

191
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,400
-What's your name, dear?
-It's Oh, ma'am.

192
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,720
-Is that comfortable enough?
-Mm.

193
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,320
That's good.

194
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,680
And who are your parents?

195
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,640
My mother's name is Malee.

196
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:30,920
Malee?

197
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,280
I'm sorry.

198
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,480
I don't remember.

199
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:37,840
That's all right.

200
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,400
It's our first time meeting, after all.

201
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,440
Why don't we get to know each other?

202
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,320
Here.

203
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,880
Do you remember who this is?

204
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,760
That's right.

205
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,800
-Does he look familiar?
-Is this his name?

206
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,160
That's right.

207
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,440
And what about this one?

208
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,120
She has long hair.

209
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,360
-She seems familiar.
-She has fair skin.

210
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,480
Do I know her?

211
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,600
Yes.

212
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,680
Do you remember her?

213
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:19,800
I like them.

214
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,360
Ms. Song,

215
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,680
are you really moving back here?

216
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,160
Is there a problem?

217
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:32,800
No,

218
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,360
I was just surprised.

219
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,160
What's so surprising?

220
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:39,160
Well, you usually stay in the city.

221
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,160
Moving back here all of a sudden…

222
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,560
Don't tell me

223
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,600
you don't trust the new nurse?

224
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,520
Or are you worried Mr. Sam will hit on her?

225
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,120
Or that she'll flirt with Mr. Sam?

226
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,040
Or--

227
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,520
I'll stop.

228
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,120
Aren't you going to the office?

229
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:57,720
No.

230
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,840
I'll work from here today.

231
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:13,160
You're going to work here?

232
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:14,560
Mm-hmm.

233
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:17,160
But you have a study.

234
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,240
A change of scenery

235
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,880
will help keep me motivated.

236
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,280
As you like.

237
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,120
What's in the blue box?

238
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,680
Madam's medication for after breakfast.

239
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:07,440
Hmm.

240
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,720
And the yellow one?

241
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,080
After lunch.

242
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:22,080
I see.

243
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:25,600
And the purple one?

244
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,800
Ms. Kasira,

245
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,760
are you here to work or to inspect me?

246
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,440
Slacking off?

247
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:38,960
Madam is asleep,

248
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,880
and I have the intercom with me.

249
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,080
Talking back, are we?

250
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,240
How shameless.

251
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,280
I thought you were only pretending,

252
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,600
but now you're shameless too.

253
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,040
Think whatever you want.

254
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:56,040
There's nothing I can do about it anyway.

255
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,480
Only 119 days left.

256
00:17:58,560 --> 00:17:59,720
I guess I'll endure it.

257
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,120
Do whatever you want.

258
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,040
Fine.

259
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,080
There.

260
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,440
That's what I wanted to do.

261
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:02,160
You're not even bothered.

262
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:05,000
You must have really thick skin.

263
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:19,400
Go ahead. Play the victim.

264
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,840
I'm good at hurting people.

265
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:04,200
I'm not as stupid as I was back then.

266
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:09,880
Cream,

267
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:11,160
where's the nurse?

268
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,520
She's in her room.

269
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:14,960
Go get her.

270
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:46,160
You called for me?

271
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,160
Eat with me.

272
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,880
I've already eaten in the kitchen.

273
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,360
Your job is to follow orders,

274
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,960
not defy them.

275
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:57,920
My only responsibility is to take care of Madam.

276
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,440
But I'm the one paying you.

277
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:03,680
Have you forgotten?

278
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,360
I don't like being disobeyed.

279
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:10,800
So don't make me angry,

280
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:12,120
or you'll regret it.

281
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:23,840
-Cream.
-Yes?

282
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,480
Set another place.

283
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,360
Of course.

284
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,560
You may leave.

285
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:10,600
Sorry?

286
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,920
Leave us.

287
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:16,080
Yes.

288
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,000
Ms. Kasira.

289
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:05,880
Eat.

290
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,920
Eat it.

291
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:14,400
If you won't eat on your own,

292
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:16,160
I'll shove it down your throat.

293
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,640
Don't think I wouldn't dare.

294
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,400
I'm done.

295
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:37,120
Are you satisfied?

296
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:38,560
I'll be going.

297
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:18,600
How long is she going to keep tormenting me?

298
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:24,680
Just a few more days until I get a break.

299
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,520
Hang in there.

300
00:27:39,320 --> 00:27:40,640
-Cream,
-Yeah?

301
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:42,200
Do you need a hand?

302
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:43,600
No.

303
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:49,720
And... don't you need to go downstairs
and prepare breakfast for Ms. Song?

304
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:50,560
No need.

305
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:52,480
Ms. Song has already left for work.

306
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,760
I'm off now.

307
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:09,640
Hey, are you working tonight?

308
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:11,480
I just got off.

309
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,680
Is something wrong?

310
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:15,800
Tomorrow's my day off.

311
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:17,600
Want to grab dinner?

312
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:19,600
I have so much to tell you.

313
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:23,440
It's about Song, isn't it?

314
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:26,640
Mm-hmm.

315
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,800
Then

316
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,320
let's meet around 7 p.m.

317
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:30,560
Where are you now?

318
00:28:31,080 --> 00:28:32,320
I'm around Phutthamonthon.

319
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:33,320
Perfect.

320
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:34,520
There's a popular place

321
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:36,120
with great reviews around there.

322
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:37,320
I'll send you the location.

323
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,800
Okay.

324
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,160
See you.

325
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:41,320
Yeah, see you.

326
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:42,520
Mm.

327
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,680
Here you go.

328
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:55,760
Thank you.

329
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:10,560
Can I get a whiskey on the rocks?

330
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:11,840
Right away.

331
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,520
Have you been here long?

332
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,240
Can I buy you a drink?

333
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:29,760
I'm good, thanks.

334
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:42,440
This place?

335
00:29:43,040 --> 00:29:43,680
Yes.

336
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,840
The clients requested to meet here.

337
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,040
They said it has a famous signature dish.

338
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,440
If it's what they want, so be it.

339
00:29:50,760 --> 00:29:52,160
Have they arrived yet?

340
00:29:52,720 --> 00:29:54,200
They're in the parking lot.

341
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:56,280
We'll wait and go in with them.

342
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,160
Yes.

343
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:06,600
Are you here alone?

344
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,000
This way, please.

345
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:09,360
I'm waiting for a friend.

346
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:19,560
I think

347
00:30:20,080 --> 00:30:21,680
we should head to the table first, Mr. Nont.

348
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:22,760
Sure.

349
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:44,680
That looks good.

350
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:47,160
This is their signature dish.

351
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,040
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

352
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:53,440
Another one, please.

353
00:30:53,520 --> 00:30:54,560
Sure.

354
00:30:58,520 --> 00:30:59,640
Here you go.

355
00:31:00,040 --> 00:31:01,000
Thank you.

356
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:02,080
Let me take this.

357
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:09,240
Hey, where are you?

358
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:11,320
My cat is missing!

359
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:13,160
I don't think I can make it.

360
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:14,480
I'm so sorry!

361
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,280
Don't worry.

362
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:18,720
We can meet another time.

363
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:21,080
I hope you find your cat soon.

364
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:23,560
Thanks.

365
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,800
Bye.

366
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:37,200
Check, please.

367
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,240
Sure. Just a moment.

368
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,800
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

369
00:31:48,120 --> 00:31:49,160
Let me treat you.

370
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,640
Maybe we can go somewhere else.

371
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:52,760
No need.

372
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:54,160
I can pay for myself.

373
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:55,520
We don't even know each other.

374
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:56,840
But I want to get to know you.

375
00:32:32,120 --> 00:32:34,040
Come on. Let's go together.

376
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:39,160
Let go of me.

377
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:41,040
I'm not going anywhere with you.
I don't even know you.

378
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,160
Excuse me.

379
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:46,960
Please excuse us.

380
00:32:48,080 --> 00:32:49,040
You're drunk.

381
00:32:49,440 --> 00:32:50,840
-Let go!
-Don't struggle.

382
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:51,920
Let me go!

383
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,640
This has nothing to do with you.

384
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:56,760
She's mine.

385
00:32:56,840 --> 00:32:58,120
So I have to get involved.

386
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:01,480
Deal with this,

387
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,880
and take care of Mr. Nont.

388
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:04,480
Of course.

389
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:55,520
Why did you get so drunk?

390
00:33:56,440 --> 00:33:58,760
You have a boyfriend,
yet you're still flirting with everyone?

391
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,080
What's that about?

392
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:02,000
Were you looking for your next target?

393
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:06,480
How did you turn out like this?

394
00:34:08,040 --> 00:34:10,400
Listen to yourself!

395
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:13,320
Are you trying to kill me

396
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,719
with your words?

397
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:16,800
You--

398
00:34:19,239 --> 00:34:20,719
You keep cursing at me!

399
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:22,639
Are you crazy, huh?

400
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:25,400
Who are you calling crazy?

401
00:34:25,719 --> 00:34:28,000
You think you're the only one who got hurt?

402
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:29,920
Do you know…

403
00:34:31,239 --> 00:34:32,840
I…

404
00:34:35,560 --> 00:34:36,600
I…

405
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:39,159
didn't actually want to break up.

406
00:34:43,159 --> 00:34:44,560
I did it…

407
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:47,320
because…

408
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:50,080
because…

409
00:34:50,159 --> 00:34:51,320
because…

410
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:56,520
Huh?

411
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:57,880
Oh?

412
00:34:58,760 --> 00:34:59,440
Oh!

413
00:35:01,080 --> 00:35:02,080
Because of what?

414
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:03,360
Wake up!

415
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,200
What the…

416
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:13,960
She's fallen asleep.

417
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:26,320
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

418
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:28,840
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

419
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:32,320
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

420
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:37,560
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

421
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:40,880
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

422
00:35:40,960 --> 00:35:45,120
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

423
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:52,400
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

424
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:59,680
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

425
00:36:28,120 --> 00:36:28,720
Hey!

426
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,320
Are you pretending to be asleep?

427
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:49,880
How can you kick me like that?

428
00:37:18,520 --> 00:37:19,480
Hello?

429
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:21,080
Oh?

430
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:24,480
Where are you?
You said you'd come home last night.

431
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:31,480
Oh?

432
00:37:32,160 --> 00:37:33,160
Uh…

433
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:35,040
Ong,

434
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:37,920
I'll call you back.

435
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:41,360
Uh, okay.

436
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:27,640
About last night…

437
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:30,240
-I'd like to--
-That's how you roll, huh?

438
00:38:32,720 --> 00:38:34,720
Sorry for interrupting.

439
00:38:35,560 --> 00:38:38,560
I was just worried you'd bring home some germs
and infect my mother.

440
00:38:42,640 --> 00:38:43,760
Don't worry.

441
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:46,320
I'll take care of myself.

442
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:49,920
I won't let my personal needs
cause any more trouble.

443
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:53,240
Thank you for letting me stay here.

444
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,120
No problem.

445
00:38:57,680 --> 00:39:00,240
I bring women here all the time.

446
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,840
But don't expect me to drive you home.

447
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,760
ONG

448
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:14,600
A new fling?

449
00:39:17,360 --> 00:39:18,360
Go on.

450
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:29,160
Then I'll get going.

451
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,720
Anything else for me to sign?

452
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,320
That's everything.

453
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,360
And meetings?

454
00:39:58,720 --> 00:39:59,840
Nothing else today.

455
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:05,680
Okay.

456
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:07,400
I'm heading to my mother's place.

457
00:40:07,480 --> 00:40:08,960
Call me if anything comes up.

458
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:10,880
Yes, Ms. Song.

459
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:20,960
Going there again…

460
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:26,880
Five.

461
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:28,640
-Six.
-Six.

462
00:40:29,640 --> 00:40:30,680
Seven.

463
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:32,480
Well done.

464
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:34,560
Eight.

465
00:40:35,560 --> 00:40:36,840
A little further.

466
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:39,360
-Nine.
-Nine.

467
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:41,200
Good job, ma'am!

468
00:40:43,120 --> 00:40:44,280
Ten.

469
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:45,760
A bit higher.

470
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,320
About this high?

471
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:49,440
Yes.

472
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:53,760
-Thirteen.
-Thirteen.

473
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:55,520
Fourteen.

474
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:57,000
Hello, Ms. Song.

475
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,440
It's your second daughter, ma'am.

476
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:17,840
Song!

477
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:24,720
How are you, honey?

478
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:26,520
Mom, have you eaten?

479
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,400
Hmm…

480
00:41:30,680 --> 00:41:31,720
I have.

481
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:34,360
That's right. I have.

482
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:37,200
Dr. Smith and Oh

483
00:41:37,280 --> 00:41:39,240
have been taking good care of me.

484
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:40,760
Thank you.

485
00:41:43,520 --> 00:41:46,000
They're so sweet.

486
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:48,040
And they look good together.

487
00:41:49,080 --> 00:41:50,280
Don't you think so?

488
00:41:58,400 --> 00:42:00,760
I'll see Dr. Smith out first, Mom.

489
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:02,840
That's nice of you.

490
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:05,200
Thank you so much, Dr. Smith.

491
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:07,160
Of course, ma'am.

492
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:09,880
I'll be going now.

493
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:11,520
-All right.
-Goodbye.

494
00:42:13,360 --> 00:42:14,760
See you later, Oh.

495
00:42:17,160 --> 00:42:18,760
Let me lower the bed for you.

496
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:19,840
Thanks.

497
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:23,640
Just a little lower.

498
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:24,960
Of course.

499
00:42:25,040 --> 00:42:27,000
-Is this low enough?
-That's good.

500
00:42:39,440 --> 00:42:41,360
How's my mother doing?

501
00:42:41,880 --> 00:42:44,560
Her Alzheimer's symptoms
seem to have improved.

502
00:42:44,960 --> 00:42:46,800
Her muscles haven't wasted away,

503
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:49,320
and she hasn't developed any pressure sores.

504
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:56,280
When will you come here next?

505
00:42:57,800 --> 00:42:59,240
As scheduled, next week.

506
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:01,400
Then stick to the schedule.

507
00:43:01,480 --> 00:43:02,960
Don't come before then.

508
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:06,600
Oh, okay.

509
00:43:09,720 --> 00:43:10,600
Then…

510
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:12,280
I'll walk you to your car.

511
00:43:13,120 --> 00:43:13,720
Thanks.

512
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:17,280
I'll be going now, Ms. Song.

513
00:43:19,560 --> 00:43:20,320
Let's go.

514
00:43:29,520 --> 00:43:30,200
Oh,

515
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:32,600
I was so busy checking on Madam

516
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:34,160
that I forgot to tell you something.

517
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:37,120
Ong brought your mother in
for a checkup this morning.

518
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:39,560
Her blood test results
are better than last time.

519
00:43:40,760 --> 00:43:44,000
Her blood counts
have also returned to acceptable levels.

520
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:46,680
There are no new abnormalities

521
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:49,560
or signs of infection.

522
00:43:50,320 --> 00:43:52,280
That means the treatment
has been working so far.

523
00:43:52,440 --> 00:43:53,400
Really?

524
00:43:53,680 --> 00:43:54,480
Yes.

525
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:57,520
But she still needs to take her medication

526
00:43:58,160 --> 00:43:59,920
and attend all her follow-up appointments.

527
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:02,240
She also needs to avoid infections.

528
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:04,640
If she has a fever or feels unwell,

529
00:44:04,640 --> 00:44:06,480
bring her to the hospital right away.

530
00:44:07,680 --> 00:44:09,520
Thank you so much, Smith.

531
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:18,680
I promised, didn't I?

532
00:44:18,680 --> 00:44:20,760
I'd do my best to look after her.

533
00:44:29,120 --> 00:44:30,000
See you.

534
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:31,440
See you.

535
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:05,160
Your smile disappears the moment you see me.

536
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:08,680
What did Smith do to make you smile like that?

537
00:45:10,880 --> 00:45:13,040
You must be dying to become a doctor's wife.

538
00:45:24,600 --> 00:45:26,680
How long are you going to keep walking away?

539
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:27,960
I don't want to fight.

540
00:45:28,040 --> 00:45:29,160
But I do.

541
00:45:29,280 --> 00:45:30,800
Are you insane?

542
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:32,800
Please get out of my room.

543
00:45:33,160 --> 00:45:34,240
Right.

544
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:36,240
You're quick to throw me out.

545
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:38,600
If it were Smith, you'd--

546
00:45:38,600 --> 00:45:39,440
That's right!

547
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:41,560
If it were him, it'd be better than this.

548
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:42,560
Satisfied?

549
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:53,880
At least he respects me,

550
00:45:55,000 --> 00:45:56,680
doesn't look down on me,

551
00:45:57,280 --> 00:45:58,840
and doesn't use force against me!

552
00:46:48,120 --> 00:46:49,880
So you really don't want me anymore?

553
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:56,080
♪ I want to tell you so you'll understand ♪

554
00:46:56,160 --> 00:47:00,160
♪ But how much longer ♪

555
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:05,000
♪ Can I keep all these words inside? ♪

556
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:09,840
♪ Every time we meet ♪

557
00:47:10,520 --> 00:47:13,080
♪ How can I keep pretending… ♪

558
00:47:14,520 --> 00:47:15,600
Cream called.

559
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,320
Mr. Sam is back at the house.

560
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:19,400
A used item

561
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:21,400
shouldn't even cost this much.

562
00:47:22,080 --> 00:47:23,520
I've even thrown in an extra.

563
00:47:24,160 --> 00:47:25,760
You're not the Song I knew.

564
00:47:26,160 --> 00:47:27,760
Stop acting innocent.

565
00:47:27,840 --> 00:47:28,760
Get out!

566
00:47:28,840 --> 00:47:30,280
What's wrong with you?

567
00:47:30,360 --> 00:47:31,680
I said get out!

568
00:47:32,800 --> 00:47:34,240
If you hate me this much,

569
00:47:34,240 --> 00:47:35,960
why keep me here as your eyesore?

570
00:47:36,080 --> 00:47:38,000
A hired hand has no right to ask me that.

571
00:47:39,840 --> 00:47:41,760
Oh? What's wrong? Oh!

572
00:47:42,080 --> 00:47:44,560
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

573
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:48,120
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

574
00:47:48,200 --> 00:47:53,320
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

575
00:47:53,400 --> 00:47:56,520
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

576
00:47:56,600 --> 00:48:01,040
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

577
00:48:01,120 --> 00:48:09,240
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

578
00:48:09,240 --> 00:48:15,240
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪
